      "text": "Fig. 6. Fibrillin-1 expression in cultured cardiac ﬁbroblasts. Quiescent cardiac ﬁbroblasts were stimulated for 48 h by increasing concentrations of ANG II (10   10 -10   8 mol/l) ( A ) or TGF  1 (10   13 -10   10 mol/l) ( B ). SDS-soluble ﬁbrillin-1 was analyzed by Western blot analysis ( A ); ﬁbrillin-1, collagen type I, and ﬁbronectin deposition were measured by a in-cell-based assay ( B ). Data were normalized to GAPDH ( A ) or   -actin ( B ). n   4 in A and n   6 in B . Results are representative of 3 experiments. * P   0.05 vs. quiescent cells. Quantiﬁcation of myocardial ﬁbrillin-1/S16 mRNA content by real-time RTPCR ( C ) is expressed as n -fold increase relative to nonstimulated cardiac ﬁbroblasts (run in duplicate). Quiescent cardiac ﬁbroblasts were stimulated for 48 h with ANG II (10   8 mol/l) or TGF  1 (1.5   10   10 mol/l). n   4 experiments. * P   0.05 vs. quiescent cells.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
